WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.493
Checks before you trust it.

2
00:00:01.773 --> 00:00:05.912
A better prompt raises the odds of good output; it does not guarantee it.

3
00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:08.837
Every technique here comes with a check you can run.

4
00:00:09.117 --> 00:00:13.277
If you asked for a format, parse it in code and reject what doesn’t parse.

5
00:00:13.557 --> 00:00:17.077
If you asked for quotes, confirm each quote appears in the source.

6
00:00:17.357 --> 00:00:20.472
If you gave categories, confirm the label is one of them.

7
00:00:20.752 --> 00:00:33.552
Prompting and verification are two halves of one job, and the rest of this week is about doing both systematically: examples and reasoning in lesson 5, then a test-driven way to iterate in lesson 6.
